//? Title: Levenshtein recursive integer coding
//? Subtitle: Actual block spans, the original10001-value round trip and checked malformed prefixes
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A recursive length code makes a binary integer self-delimiting by describing the
lengths needed to reconstruct it. We inspect actual emitted/read spans, retain
the original codewords, round trip and Exp-Golomb length comparison, and fix the
native decoder’s unsafe handling of truncated or unrepresentable prefixes. The
code supports every unsigned64 value, including zero; it is unrelated to a text
edit-distance computation.
)

\toc

> Recursive lengths and a unary depth

Zero is0. For positive n, remove the leading1 from its binary representation,
retain the remaining m=floor(log2(n)) bits, and repeat on m until the current
value is1. If there are C such levels, emit C ones followed by0 and then the
retained blocks from outermost length to original value. The leading1 of each
block is implicit.

For n10, the actual level values are10,3,1. Reversed emission has the width0
implicit1 level, then one explicit bit1 reconstructing3, then three bits010
reconstructing10. The word is11101010. The native record includes the width0
level even though it emits no payload bits.

Decoding reads C, starts at N1, and repeats C−1 times: read N explicit low bits
and prepend1. Thus each next block length is known before reading it. This
establishes unique prefix decoding, provided every delimiter and block is
present and the represented value fits the chosen integer domain. It does not
make damaged streams error-correcting.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/levcode_blocks.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto e = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_encode_trace({10});
    auto d = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_decode_trace(e.bits, 1);
    std::string bits;
    for (bool b : e.bits)
        bits += b ? '1' : '0';
    std::print("Actual emitted bits {}; actual decoded value {}.\n\n| actual block start | actual explicit " "width | actual reconstructed value |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               bits, d.values[0]);
    for (auto &b : d.words[0].blocks)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", b.begin, b.width, b.value);
    dm::graphics::Diagram g;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < d.words[0].blocks.size(); ++i) {
        auto &b = d.words[0].blocks[i];
        auto id = std::to_string(i);
        g.node(id, {6. * i, 0},
               std::format("Actual decoded level{}\nwidth{}; value{}", i,
                           b.width, b.value));
        if (i)
            g.edge(std::to_string(i - 1), id);
    }
    g.save_svg("build/levcode_blocks.svg");
}
```
