> Original codewords and complete round trip

Retain original values0,1,2,4,7,16,100, then encode and decode every integer
from0 through10000 inclusive. That is10001 values, correcting the earlier loose
wording “ten thousand.” The complete exact-count decoder now throws if the
requested prefix is incomplete; it never silently returns fewer values. The
figure shows actual codeword lengths on the original small values. Bit strings
are ordinary short textual codewords, not image data.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/levcode_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_encode_trace({0, 1, 2, 4, 7, 16, 100});
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| original integer | actual emitted codeword | actual bit length |\n| ---: | --- | ---: " "|\n");
    for (auto &w : t.words) {
        std::string code;
        for (std::size_t j = w.begin; j < w.end; ++j)
            code += t.bits[j] ? '1' : '0';
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", w.value, code, w.end - w.begin);
        x.push_back(w.value);
        y.push_back(w.end - w.begin);
    }
    std::vector<std::uint64_t> v;
    for (std::uint64_t n = 0; n <= 10000; ++n)
        v.push_back(n);
    auto bits = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_encode(v);
    auto d = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_decode_trace(bits, int(v.size()));
    std::print("\nActual round-trip values {}; equality {}; actual emitted bits {}; actual consumed bits " "{}; actual read visits {}.\n",
               v.size(), d.values == v, bits.size(), d.consumed_bits,
               d.work.bit_visits);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual codeword lengths", {37, 99, 235}, 6).title(
        "Original small-value recursive codewords").x_label(
        "original nonnegative integer").y_label("actual emitted bits").save_svg(
        "build/levcode_original.svg");
}
```
