> Length growth and the original comparison

For n>0, let n_0=n and n_{j+1}=floor(log2(n_j)) until n_{C-1}=1. The actual word
length is

$$\ell(n)=C+1+\sum_{j=0}^{C-1}\lfloor\log_2(n_j)\rfloor.$$
\alttext(Length equals the unary-depth prefix and delimiter plus every explicit recursive binary payload width.)

The dominant term is log2(n), with smaller iterated-log overhead. Calling the
whole length “iterated logarithmic” was incorrect. Original order0 Exp-Golomb
comparison values are retained. That comparator supports zero by coding n+1, so
it is not literally Elias gamma on positive n. The actual crossover is data
dependent; neither code universally wins on small values or all source
distributions. The plot uses real emitted lengths, without an entropy or
optimal-compression claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/levcode_lengths.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, l, g;
    std::print("| original integer | actual Levenshtein bits | actual order0 Exp-Golomb bits |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::uint64_t n : {1ULL, 4ULL, 16ULL, 64ULL, 256ULL, 1024ULL, 16384ULL,
                            1000000ULL, 1000000000ULL}) {
        auto a =
            dm::algorithms::levenshtein_encode({n}), b =
            dm::algorithms::exp_golomb_encode({n}, 0);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", n, a.size(), b.size());
        x.push_back(std::log2(double(n)));
        l.push_back(a.size());
        g.push_back(b.size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, l, "actual Levenshtein", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, l, "",
                                                                {37, 99, 235}, 4).line(x, g, "actual Exp-Golomb0", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, g, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4).y_limits(0, 78).title("Original measured recursive-code length comparison").x_label("log2(original integer)").y_label("actual emitted bits").save_svg("build/levcode_lengths.svg");
}
```
