> Exact prefixes and malformed controls

The parser checks every unary delimiter and binary block extent, rejects unary
depth beyond the unsigned64 domain and checks block width at most63 before any
shift or indexed payload read. Exactly count words must parse. Negative count
fails; count0 reads no bits. Unread trailing bits are allowed by the prefix
contract and are not validated or counted as visits. The new trace owns that
full original tail and reports consumed_bits separately.

For the actual emitted word of10, test every strict truncation, including the
empty input. Each must fail to produce the requested one complete value. A
prefix0 followed by an unfinished1 tail successfully parses one zero and
consumes only its first bit. These are real guarded parser calls; the plot
reports observed rejection statuses, not simulated decoder behavior.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/levcode_guards.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto bits = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_encode({10});
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual supplied prefix bits | actual request rejected |\n| ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t k = 0; k <= bits.size(); ++k) {
        std::vector<bool> prefix(bits.begin(), bits.begin() + k);
        bool rejected = false;
        try {
            auto v = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_decode(prefix, 1);
        } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
            rejected = true;
        }
        std::print("| {} | {} |\n", k, rejected);
        x.push_back(k);
        y.push_back(rejected ? 1 : 0);
    }
    auto d = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_decode_trace({false, true}, 1);
    std::print("\nActual prefix value {}; actual consumed bits {}; original owned stream bits {}; actual " "visited bits {}.\n",
               d.values[0], d.consumed_bits, d.bits.size(), d.work.bit_visits);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual rejected status", {220, 38, 38}, 6).y_limits(-.15,
                                                                        1.5).title("Actual checked parsing of every truncated10 word").x_label("supplied actual prefix bits").y_label("actual rejection:1 yes,0 no").save_svg("build/levcode_guards.svg");
}
```
